prompt.text:
Repair the complete source below. `encodeFields(fields)` accepts an array containing only strings; otherwise it throws `TypeError`. It returns the fields in their original order, each surrounded by double quotes and separated by semicolons. Inside every field, each backslash must become two backslashes and every double quote must be preceded by one backslash. Backslashes are escaped before quotes. An empty array returns the empty string. The input must not be mutated. Return a corrected complete source file exporting exactly `{ encodeFields }`.

```javascript
"use strict";

function encodeFields(fields) {
  if (!Array.isArray(fields) || fields.some((field) => typeof field !== "string")) {
    throw new TypeError("fields must be an array of strings");
  }

  return fields
    .map((field) => "\"" + field.replace(/\\/g, "\\\\").replace("\"", "\\\"") + "\"")
    .join(";");
}

module.exports = { encodeFields };
```

